WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.860
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit 5: Actions and Activities.

2
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:05.680
Welcome to Unit 5!

3
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.360
This unit is all about actions and
activities — the things people DO.

4
00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:16.220
You will learn lots of action words (verbs)
such as build, discuss, protect and celebrate.

5
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.740
You will talk about things you did, using the past simple,

6
00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.440
and learn to explain why things
happened using words like because and so.

7
00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:32.040
You will put events in order with First, Next, Then and
Finally, ask Wh- questions, and share your ideas politely.

8
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:37.820
By the end, you will be ready to read this
unit's story, “The Wall Behind the Garden”,

9
00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:41.300
where a class of children work
together to build something special.

10
00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:47.200
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

11
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.520
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name
and use many action words, such as build, listen,

12
00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:55.860
protect and celebrate.

13
00:00:55.860 --> 00:01:01.500
you will also talk about things you did, using
the past simple (built, listened, celebrated).

14
00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:05.600
you will also explain why something
happened, using because and so.

15
00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.940
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

16
00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:16.640
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
discuss, listen, offer, build, complete, remove.

17
00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:22.020
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

18
00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:25.270
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

19
00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:29.800
The reading sequence includes A
Busy Saturday and Helping Hands.

20
00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:31.180
Read actively.

21
00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:36.040
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

22
00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:40.000
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

23
00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:44.140
The first language focus is The Past Simple Tense.

24
00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:49.280
We use the past simple to talk about actions
that already happened and are finished.

25
00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.360
It helps us tell stories and share things we did.

26
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:59.600
In this unit's story, the children built a wall —
that already happened, so we say built, not build.

27
00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:06.120
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

28
00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:10.300
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 — Tell What You Did.

29
00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:14.840
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

30
00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:18.240
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

31
00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:21.470
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

32
00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.360
You are ready to begin.

33
00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:29.120
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

34
00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.720
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

35
00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:37.700
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
